[gd_scene load_steps=14 format=3 uid="uid://cxabmain1234"]

; WHAT THIS IS, AND WHY
;
; The Design Lab - the screen where the player assembles a unit from a
; hull + module parts. The active model is FLOATING, unsupported, at
; y = 2.5. Far below it the shared LabEnvironment draws a cutting mat
; and a few kraft-cardboard model-kit boxes for context. The camera's
; DOF eats the mat and the boxes heavily; the player mostly sees the
; model sharp and the lower half of the frame as a green-and-white
; blur that reads as "workshop below".
;
; Why y = 2.5 for the hull:
;   * The placer's lift site (hull.position.y = fitted_size.y/2 +
;     stage_y_offset) puts the hull's bottom at y = stage_y_offset,
;     so stage_y_offset = 2.0 places the bottom at 2.0 and the centre
;     at 2.5 (for a 1u-tall hull). Anything 0.5+ would work; 2.0
;     reads as "clearly elevated, not on the floor" without the
;     pedestal-on-pedestal look.
;   * There's no longer a clipping constraint - the mat is at y = -20,
;     well below the worst-case camera dip of 4.76u below the pivot
;     at min_zoom + max_pitch. The model height is now a design
;     choice (how high should the floating model sit?) rather than a
;     math one.
;
; DOF notes:
;   * CameraAttributesPractical is wired in below; designer_camera.gd
;     updates dof_blur_far_distance on zoom so the focal point tracks
;     the model. dof_blur_amount is set high (0.25, well above Battle's
;     0.06) because here the mat IS the subject to be blurred,
;     not just a distant landscape band.
;
; WORKBENCH SWAP (2026-08-18): the player enters the Armor Station
; (paint workspace) by clicking PAINT STATION in the toolbar. The
; left parts bin swaps to a paint toolkit (UI_ArmorStationPanel),
; the cutting mat environment hides and the wood-desktop + paint
; supplies environment (PaintStationEnvironment) becomes visible,
; and the model slides over to hover above the workbench. The
; pan_blur overlay covers all three changes, so the player sees
; a single "turn to the workbench" gesture instead of three
; discrete ones. The reverse pan undoes the same swaps.

